<p>Driving for Uber or Lyft is the side hustle most people try first: you already have a car and a phone, sign-up takes days, and you can cash out the same day you drive. It is also the side hustle most people overestimate, because the number in the app is not what you keep. This guide covers the 2026 requirements, the real math on hourly earnings after expenses, the insurance gap that catches new drivers, when to drive, how to multi-app, and how taxes work.</p>

